<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6417" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνα-δείκνῡμι</span></b> , also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνα-ύω</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Plu.
			2.417e
		</span></i>: lon. aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έδεξα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
				</span></i>
			 (v. infr.): pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-δέδειχα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					21.21.3
				</span></i>
			: (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δείκνυμι</span>):—<i>lift up and show, exhibit,
				display,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πύλας ἀναδεικνύναι</span>
			<i>display by opening</i> gates, i.e. <i>throw wide</i> the
			gates, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				1458
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυστοδόκος δόμος ἀναδείκνυται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					304
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναδέξαι ἀσπίδα</span>
			<i>hold</i> up shield <i>as signal,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.115
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				121
			</span></i> sq.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνέδεξε σημήιον τοῖς ἄλλοις
				ἀνάγεσθαι</span>
			<i>made</i> signal for them to put to sea, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				7.128
			</span></i>; [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μίλητος] Θαλῆν ἀ.,</span> on
			a statue, Epigr. ap. <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				1.34
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>notify,</i> esp. <i>proclaim</i> any one as elected to
			office, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὑτὸν ἀναδεδειχὼς βασιλέα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					4.48.3
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τινὰ μέγιστον</span>
			<i>make</i> him the greatest man, <i><span class="en">
				22.4.3
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνέδειξεν ἑτέρους ἑβδομήκοντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
					10.1
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναδεδεῖχθαι τὸ ἱερὸν ἄσυλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>SIG</u>
					630.23
				</span></i>
			 (Delph., <span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>dedicate,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ Διὶ ταῦρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>SIG</u>
					589.6
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Magn.
			</span></i> Mae., <span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν Πιερίδα ταῖς θεαῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					9.2.25
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέατρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Pomp.</u>
					52
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱερά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.340
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πόλεμον</span>
			<i>declare</i> war, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				742.12
			</span></i> (Ephesus, <span class="entity">i B. C.</span>).</div>
